      "problem": "Given that $6{x}^{6}-13{x}^{3}-8=(a{x}^{3}-8)(2{x}^{3}+b)$ where $a$ and $b$ are integers, find the value of $a+b.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can introduce a new variable $z={x}^{3}$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{6}-13{x}^{3}-8 & =6{({x}^{3})}^{2}-13({x}^{3})-8 \\\\  & =6{z}^{2}-13z-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{z}^{2}-13z-8 & =(3z-8)(2z+1) \\\\  & =(3{x}^{3}-8)(2{x}^{3}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $a=3$, $b=1$ and $a+b=4.$",
