      "problem": "The trinomial ${p}^{4}+2{p}^{2}-15$ is equivalent to",
      "worked_solution": "We can introduce a new variable $z={p}^{2}$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{4}+2{p}^{2}-15 & ={({p}^{2})}^{2}+2({p}^{2})-15 \\\\  & ={z}^{2}+2z-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}+2z-15 & =(z-3)(z+5) \\\\  & =({p}^{2}-3)({p}^{2}+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
